Controller/UI:

* Clear stats support, clear all and clear per interface.

* We should add a troubleshooting tab, the initial functionality should be to check db rule
state vs agent rule state and we should alert if there are discrepencies. Taking this further
we should have an option to restore from either DB version or agent version, this should
push the rules to the node AND reconcile all rule versions (DB should match agent). The second functionality should be a function to export all rules from the DB into json format, offer
the ability to export per node, per interface, or all.

Agent:

Needs cpu affinity support.

Security / PKI:

* CSR-based mTLS issuance ("Phase 3" in security/ca.rs, node_registry/mod.rs,
  agent/enrollment/mod.rs; also referenced as "future phase" in docs/tpm.md).
  Today the controller mints both key and cert on approval and ships them to
  the agent. The agent already builds and signs a CSR during enrollment with an
  ephemeral key — that CSR is currently discarded. Pending work: have the agent
  generate the CSR key inside the TPM (so the on-the-wire mTLS key never leaves
  hardware) and have the controller sign that CSR instead of generating its own
  keypair. Touches enrollment proto, agent identity backends, controller CA,
  and cert-rotation logic.

* TLS-layer cert revocation enforcement (extends "Phase 4"). Serial capture +
  the connect-time revocation check landed alongside this TODO (mgmt Hello
  rejects when the stored serial is in revoked_certs). Still missing: extract
  the serial from the *presented* peer cert at the TLS layer (tonic
  TlsConnectInfo + an x509 parse of peer_certs) and reject there. Without this,
  a stale cert presented after a row was tampered back to Active, or a cert
  whose row has been re-issued with a new serial, would not be caught by the
  serial check alone — only by the status check.

